{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA: test.yml used workflow concurrency group test-${{ github.ref }} with cancel-in-progress true. On main both schedule and workflow_dispatch evaluate github.ref to refs/heads/main, so the two distinct main-health readings share one cancellation key and either can silently cancel the other. RED evidence: added policy/report tests first; schedule-vs-manual group separation failed because both rendered test-refs/heads/main, and cancelled/skipped report failed because render returned RED instead of UNAVAILABLE. Fix hypothesis: add event_name to the group to preserve same-event/ref bounding while separating schedule from manual, and render incomplete gate results as UNAVAILABLE."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788988788659046001,"uuid":"269ea5c7-e353-4ee7-8376-27cce5a361ef"}